A||||2||crzyone||Engine Trouble||||1||
Z||000000||crzyone||01-24-2001||11:08 PM||||Hey there, I have a problem with my Iron Duke..  I was driving it the other day, shut it off and left it overnight.  The next day when I went to start it it didn't fire or anything.  When I poured gas down the air intake it fired and ran for a couple seconds so I thought the problem was fuel pump or filter.  Both are good.  Has anyone had something similar happen?   ||||reg||1
Z||000001||crzyone||01-25-2001||12:05 AM||||I have another question.  Wherabouts is the oil pressure sensor on the V6?  I looked the other day and couldn't see one.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||01-25-2001||08:30 AM||||The v-6 oil pressure switch is between the water pump and the battery on the passenger side of the engine.  It is a cylindrical can mounted vertically.  It is connected to the oil filter housing via a long steel tube and it has a wire connector on top.  The steel tube snakes its way down under the A/C compressor.||||reg||1
